Column F is "Principle" and E holds the interest from IPMT. D is the monthly payment from PMT, which comes out negative. E is also negative (IPMT). The balance in G is computed as G(prev)+F, so F must be negative principal paid down. G17 = D6+F17, so F17 should be the negative of the principal portion, which is the payment minus the interest. D17-E17 = PMT - IPMT = PPMT, which is negative. So G17 = D6 + PPMT gives the reduced balance.

The formula is therefore =D17-E17.

{"formula": "=D17-E17"}

